# Clock-gating pre-pass for the decimator macro.
#
# yosys clockgate skips a flop whose synchronous reset overrides its enable, and
# every register here is one (if (!rst_b) q <= 0; else if (ce) q <= d;). Writing
# the reset into the enable does not help either: yosys then infers $sdffce,
# which clockgate skips for the same reason. LibreLane runs clockgate inside its
# synthesis step with no hook before it, so this pass does the work first: the
# sync reset becomes logic (techmap sdffe_to_dffe.v), leaving the enable
# ce | reset, opt_merge shares that enable across the flops of a group, and
# clockgate puts a CGX3 in front of each group of 3 or more.
#
# Not run directly: the macro Makefile substitutes @EZ130_LIB@ with the typical
# corner of EZ130_DIR and writes the result into the macro rtl_gen/.

read_liberty -lib @EZ130_LIB@
read_verilog -sv rtl/ce_generator.sv rtl/cic_n6_d32.sv rtl/sinc2_chain.sv rtl/comp_fir.sv rtl/decimator_core.sv rtl/decimator_top.sv
hierarchy -check -top decimator_top
proc
flatten
opt_expr
opt_clean
opt_dff
opt_clean
techmap -map ../scripts/sdffe_to_dffe.v t:$sdffe t:$sdffce
opt_expr
opt_merge
opt_clean
clockgate -pos CGX3 E:CK:ECK -min_net_size 3
opt_clean
stat
write_verilog -noattr rtl_gen/decimator_top_cg.v
